///
/// WHY IT EXISTS. `LASVerifyOpt` is MEASURED to fit at Simplified Dilithium-III with 363,941
/// gas of headroom. Whether it fits at Dilithium-V was argued from arithmetic five times and
/// found unsound five times. Every defect is recorded so a sixth attempt cannot reintroduce
/// one:
///
///   1. "Execution can only grow" is not a bound. Calldata byte content is a SECOND free
///      variable; pushed the D5-favourable way (every added byte zero) with execution frozen,
///      D5 lands *under* the cap. A worst case binds only when every free variable is pushed
///      the adverse way at once.
///   2. `shake_stage_gas / block_count` does NOT lower-bound one added block: the stage total
///      also carries `init()` and the pad tail, so the quotient OVERstates per-block cost.
///   3. `SampleInBall` is not the only data-dependent stage — `_decodeZ` branches on
///      coefficient value (`if gt(f, 137935)`). Neither may be assumed to cost at least its D3
///      value at D5, so the combining script subtracts both whole.
///   4. Timing `absorbPad` at two different buffer sizes contaminates the difference:
///      `absorbPad` allocates its 168-byte pad scratch INSIDE the frame, so memory-expansion
///      gas lands in the measurement and differs with the caller's high-water mark.
///   5. The two lengths do not share a tail PATH, so the tail term cannot simply be dropped:
///      at `rem = 80` (D3) the tail copies two words AND takes the `if tb` partial-word
///      branch, while at `rem = 96` (D5) it copies three words and SKIPS that branch. The
///      difference `tail_D5 − tail_D3` is not provably non-negative, so discarding it is not
///      conservative.
///
/// HOW 4 AND 5 ARE BOTH REMOVED. They share a root cause: letting memory state vary between
/// measurements, then having to model what varied. Instead, every measurement here runs
/// against a FIXED MAX-SIZE ARENA — one buffer of the largest length, allocated identically
/// every time — and only the `len` argument to `absorbPad` changes. The free-memory pointer at
/// the start of each timed frame is therefore identical, the 168-byte scratch is allocated at
/// the same offset, and its expansion cost cancels EXACTLY in the difference. Nothing about
/// the tail has to be modelled, because the difference of two direct measurements is the
/// quantity itself, tail included.
///
/// WHAT IS MEASURED
///   preimage = pack(t) ‖ pack(w') ‖ M = 2·n·1024 + |M|, with |M| = 32 as measured on chain
///   D3 (n=6): 12,320 B      D5 (n=8): 16,416 B
///   deltaAbsorb = gas(absorbPad, 16,416) − gas(absorbPad, 12,320)
/// `permute` is measured separately as an independent fixed-cost unit (24 fixed rounds, only
/// loop-counter comparisons, no allocation, no data-dependent control flow), so `deltaAbsorb`
/// can be sanity-checked against 30 × permute rather than taken on trust — 30 being the added
/// FULL blocks, 90 → 120.
///
/// NOT COUNTED, deliberately: the digest comparison also grows (`_digestMatches` reads six
/// lanes at D3, eight at D5 — a deterministic loop with no data dependence, so it is provably
/// larger). Leaving out a provably positive term only weakens the bound, which is safe.
///
/// ⚠ Run WITHOUT `--gas-report`: the inspector is metered inside the measured frame and
/// inflates `gasleft()` deltas. Same rule as the cap gates in `LASGasBreakdown.t.sol`.
contract LASShakeGrowthTest {
    uint256 constant PREIMAGE_D3 = 12_320; // n = 6
    uint256 constant PREIMAGE_D5 = 16_416; // n = 8
    uint256 constant SHAKE256_RATE = 136;

    ShakeHarness h;

    function setUp() public {
        h = new ShakeHarness();
    }

    /// The primary measurement. Both calls allocate the same max-size arena, so the only
    /// difference between the two timed frames is the work `absorbPad` does.
    function test_absorb_growth_D3_to_D5() public {
        h.absorbGas(PREIMAGE_D3); // warm-up, discarded
        h.absorbGas(PREIMAGE_D5);

        uint256 gasD3 = h.absorbGas(PREIMAGE_D3);
        uint256 gasD5 = h.absorbGas(PREIMAGE_D5);
        require(gasD5 > gasD3, "absorb did not grow with preimage length");

        console.log("absorbPad arena bytes (identical for every measurement)", PREIMAGE_D5);
        console.log("absorbPad len D3 / D5", PREIMAGE_D3, PREIMAGE_D5);
        console.log("absorbPad gas D3", gasD3);
        console.log("absorbPad gas D5", gasD5);
        console.log("absorbPad DELTA gas D5 minus D3", gasD5 - gasD3);
    }

    /// Corroboration only. Differencing two EXPLICITLY UNROLLED runs: the difference is exactly
    /// eight more `permute` invocations, with no loop counter, comparison or jump — so it is
    /// not `permute + loop overhead`, which is what a loop-based measurement would give.
    function test_permute_unit_cost() public {
        h.permute8(); // warm-up
        h.permute16();

        uint256 g8 = h.permute8();
        uint256 g16 = h.permute16();
        require(g16 > g8, "unrolled permute did not scale");

        uint256 marginal = (g16 - g8) / 8;
        console.log("permute unrolled x8 / x16 gas", g8, g16);
        console.log("permute MARGINAL gas per call", marginal);
        console.log("30 x marginal permute (cross-check on the absorb delta)", 30 * marginal);
    }

