Confirmed against the source — you're right, and I had it wrong. [LASGasBreakdown.t.sol](evm/test/LASGasBreakdown.t.sol) measures stage `g[4]` as exactly:

```solidity
s = gasleft();
uint256 p = LASShake.init();
LASShake.absorbPad(p, prePtr, pre.length);
g[4] = s - gasleft();
```

`init() + absorbPad()`, then it stops. `_digestMatches` is not in that stage at all. And your second catch is right too: the pad-tail path doesn't *cancel* — it differs, and is **included in** the measured difference. Only memory expansion cancels.

